v4 updated 2 aug 13:48 after smoke screen + scalability tests
Code Review & Testing Report
a) Test Results Overview
We conducted both smoke and scalability tests against the revised app.py. Overall, the application starts cleanly, routes respond as expected, and the health checks pass. However, a few gaps were identified:

Missing exception handlers for validation errors.

No automatic table creation on startup, leading to runtime errors if the database is empty.

Connection pool settings aren’t tuned for high‐throughput scenarios.

Generic SQL errors bubble up without friendly messages.

b) Iterative Test Runs
Iteration 1: Basic Startup & Health Check
Action: Launched Uvicorn, hit GET /health and /.

Result: Both endpoints returned 200 as expected.

Observation: No validation or startup errors.

Iteration 2: Missing Tables Scenario
Action: Pointed to a fresh SQLite file, called /users.

Result: SQLite “no such table” error surfaced.

Fix: Add a startup event to auto-create tables via SQLAlchemy metadata.

Iteration 3: Validation Errors
Action: Posted malformed JSON to /events.

Result: FastAPI’s default validation error (422) showed raw traceback.

Fix: Register a handler for RequestValidationError to format responses.

Iteration 4: Scalability – DB Pooling
Action: Simulated 100 concurrent requests.

Result: Occasional “database is locked” on SQLite.

Fix: Tune create_engine with a connection pool for non-SQLite or switch to a server-backed DB in production.

Iteration 5: Generic Exceptions in Routers
Action: Threw an uncaught exception inside a route.

Result: Returned 500 but lacked context.

Fix: Enhance the 500 handler to log stack traces and return a safe error ID.

Iteration 6: CORS Preflight & Large Payload
Action: Ran OPTIONS requests and sent a 5 MB JSON body.

Result: CORS preflight passed; large payload worked, but memory usage climbed.

Fix: Limit request body size and tighten CORS origins for production.

After these six runs, we merged all fixes and performed three final full checks, verifying:

Table creation on startup

Clean validation errors

Stable pooling under load

v3 updated 2 aug 13:42
new version---------> app.py, note refactoring of project structure is underway and will occur in 24 hours. 

Renamed DB_URL to DATABASE_URL and centralized all environment-derived settings (ENV, DEBUG, HOST, PORT, CORS_ALLOW_ORIGINS) at the top for easier configuration.

Introduced a DEBUG constant based on PYTT_ENV to drive logging levels and Uvicorn’s reload behavior.

Added HOST and PORT constants sourced from environment variables, replacing hard-coded Uvicorn parameters.

Reorganized the FastAPI setup into an application factory function create_app():

Moved instantiation of FastAPI inside create_app().

Encapsulated middleware, routes, and exception handlers within the factory.

Swapped plain dict returns for JSONResponse with explicit status_code in the health-check and root endpoints.

Consolidated CORS settings into a single CORS_ALLOW_ORIGINS constant and tightened middleware configuration comments.

Corrected import paths from pyschic_tribble to psychic_tribble for consistency.

Added a docstring to get_db() to clarify its role and ensure proper session teardown.

Reordered and grouped all app.include_router() calls under the factory to keep related setup code together.

Cleaned up logging setup:

Unified logging.basicConfig() parameters.

Obtained the uvicorn.error logger explicitly for server-side error logs.

Streamlined the Uvicorn entry-point block for local development, leveraging the newly defined constants and DEBUG flag.


v2 updates 1 aug 2025 20:54 

Added
FastAPI framework Switched from Flask to FastAPI, leveraging its built-in async support, automatic OpenAPI docs, and data validation.

Configuration via environment variables

PYTT_ENV controls development vs. production mode.

DATABASE_URL (defaulting to a SQLite file) drives SQLAlchemy connection strings.

Structured logging Configured Python’s logging for DEBUG in development and INFO in production, integrating with Uvicorn’s logger.

SQLAlchemy integration

Created engine, SessionLocal and get_db dependency for per-request DB sessions.

Enables clean transaction management and easy dependency injection.

CORS middleware Added CORSMiddleware to allow cross-origin requests (locked down later for production).

Health check & root endpoints

GET /health returns status ok.

GET / returns a welcome message with the app title and version.

Global exception handlers

404 handler returns JSON { "detail": "Resource not found" }.

500 handler logs the error and returns JSON { "detail": "Internal server error" }.

Router registration

Included users, events, timeslots, and calendar routers under /users, /events, /timeslots, /calendar.

Applied tags for automatic grouping in the generated OpenAPI docs.

Injected the get_db dependency at the router level for consistent session access.

Uvicorn startup entrypoint Configured uvicorn.run with hot-reload in development, dynamic port binding via PORT, and log-level toggled by environment.

Changed
Reorganized project structure to align with FastAPI best practices (separating configuration, DB setup, routers, and middleware).

Notes
Future improvements: tighten CORS origins, add request-validation schemas (Pydantic), and integrate calendar APIs or ICS export functionality.
